[Chapter "Without c4"]
[Line "Against the London (2.Bf4)"]
[Opening "Queen's Pawn Game: Accelerated London System"]

{Many players skip c4 and play the London. Hit d4 with ...c5 and develop the bishop Slav-style.} 1. d4 d5 {Claim the centre.} 2. Bf4 {The London System.} 2... Nf6 {Develop.} 3. e3 c5 {Against the London, hit d4 with the c-pawn straight away.} 4. c3 Nc6 {More pressure on d4.} 5. Nd2 Bf5 {The Slav idea again: bishop out before ...e6.} 6. Ngf3 e6 {Close the chain behind the bishop.} 7. Qb3 {White attacks b7.} 7... Qc8 {Guard b7 and keep the bishop on f5.} *
